## Integrating with MeshNode

The node takes a `TransportManager` — the registry of schemes it may speak — so
the first thing to do is register yours:

```python
from src import MeshNode
from src.transports.manager import TransportManager

manager = TransportManager()
manager.register("mine", MyTransport, MyServer)
node = MeshNode(manager)
await node.start("mine://address")
await node.join("mine://other_address", code)
```

The node ships with `tcp`, `udp` and `spool`; `scripts/nmesh_node.py` builds its
manager from `src/transports/registry.py` (`register_all`), which is the single
place those three are declared.

