## Framing

TCP is a byte stream with no boundaries between messages. Your transport must
delimit packets. The recommended strategy: a 2-byte prefix (uint16 big-endian)
giving the size of the packet that follows.

```
[0x00][0x4B]  →  the next 75 bytes = one Packet
```

For datagram-oriented protocols (UDP, LoRa, BLE) no framing is needed: one
datagram = one packet.

